{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification enforces conservative, safe exploration: random_walk is used for exploration in clear states, move_forward is used only in a short commit state, and all obstacle events force explicit, one-shot turn-based recovery. Obstacle recovery states enable only the safe turn direction and never allow forward or random_walk. The supervisor ensures no ambiguous recovery, no unsafe forward, and no oscillation.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to allow modular specification.",
    "Specification automaton encodes strict safety: obstacle events preempt exploration, force explicit turn recovery, and only allow resumption of exploration when clear."
  ],
